  "generated_text": "We know that\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{ab} + \\frac{1}{ac} + \\frac{1}{ad} + \\frac{1}{bc} + \\frac{1}{bd} + \\frac{1}{cd} = \\frac{ab + ac + ad + bc + bd + cd}{abcd}.\n\\]\nBy Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\\[\na + b + c + d = -8,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + ac + ad + bc + bd + cd = 9,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc + abd + acd + bcd = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nabcd = 4.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{ab} + \\frac{1}{ac} + \\frac{1}{ad} + \\frac{1}{bc} + \\frac{1}{bd} + \\frac{1}{cd} = \\frac{ab + ac + ad + bc + bd + cd}{abcd} = \\frac{9}{4} = \\boxed{\\frac{9}{4}}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\boxed{\\frac{9}{4}}.",
